#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: lemons: 22
#> pause: 45
#> must: # command:  sed -E -f
#> must: apples: 12 units (12 units) [line 1]
#> must: lemons: 22 units (22 units) [line 8]
#> not: 1 apples 12
#> source: \2: \3
# 9. Groups and -E. Sheet: -E (or -r) uses extended regular expressions in the script.
# In the replacement \1 \2 \3 are the parenthesised groups and & is the whole match.
# With -E the parentheses and + are plain; in basic syntax they would be \( \) and \+.
# The first s/// reorders the fields; the second shows & by wrapping the number.
# Try: remove -E from #ARGS: sed now wants \( \) and the first s/// matches nothing.
#ARGS -E
s/^([0-9]+) ([a-z]+) ([0-9]+)$/\2: \3 units [line \1]/
s/[0-9]+ units/& (&)/

#DATA
1 apples 12
2 bananas 30
3 cherries 7
4 dates 16
5 figs 25
6 grapes 40
7 kiwis 18
8 lemons 22
